{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>As Aaron your brother died.</b> By the same death that you saw and desired — that Moses stripped Aaron of the first garment and dressed Elazar in it, and likewise the second, and likewise the third, and he saw his son in his glory. Moses said to him: Aaron my brother, go down below — and he went down; stretch out your hand — and he stretched; stretch out your leg — and he stretched; close your eyes — and he closed; pursed your mouth — and he pursed; and he passed on. Moses said: Happy is the one who dies by this death (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:32.763759028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}